    // Global finance: pace-of-transmission notes per scenario
    '传导节奏：金融市场可能提前交易降息；企业新项目和居民贷款的效果需等待落地。': 'Pace of transmission: financial markets may trade a rate cut in advance; the effect on new corporate projects and household loans has to wait to materialize.',
    '传导节奏：市场可能先跌后见到降息；信用修复和就业恢复也可能晚于政策转向。': 'Pace of transmission: markets may fall first and only then see rate cuts; credit repair and employment recovery may also come later than the policy turn.',
    '传导节奏：资金利率可能先变化，LPR、实际贷款、项目开工与家庭消费的响应各有时滞。': 'Pace of transmission: money-market rates may change first, while the LPR, actual loans, project starts and household consumption each respond with their own lag.',
    '传导节奏：能源价格可快速变化；成本转嫁、工资谈判和通胀预期的影响较慢。': 'Pace of transmission: energy prices can change quickly; cost pass-through, wage negotiations and inflation expectations work more slowly.',
    '传导节奏：去杠杆可能在短时间内发生；不能据此推断所有全球资产的涨跌幅。': 'Pace of transmission: deleveraging can happen in a short time; it cannot be used to infer the rise or fall of all global assets.',
